{"answer": "Gemini pods ran with no Lore MCP tools because of where the MCP config was written. Subsystem v0.11.2 wrote it to a system-scope settings file, /agent/.ai-agent/gemini-settings.json, which was pointed to by GEMINI_CLI_SYSTEM_SETTINGS_PATH. gemini-cli refuses a system settings file when its parent directory isn't owned by root, and the pod runs as uid 1000. It printed \"Security Warning: Skipping system settings file ... Parent directory is not owned by root (uid 0). Current uid: 1000\" and started with \"init … (0 tools)\". Four Gemini runs made zero MCP calls. The fix was subsystem #246 (v0.11.3). Its init step merges mcpServers into the gemini-cli user settings file, /agent/.gemini/settings.json, via `ai-agent-init mcp-settings`. This was proven on 2026-09-23 when run f0e87e9e made mcp_lore_* tool calls. I did not find what the earlier versions did before v0.11.2, so this covers only the v0.11.2 failure.", "sources": ["memory: session-summary/2026-09-23-gemini-review-mcp-refused", "memory: session-summary/2026-09-23-gemini-mcp-v0.11.3-proven", "re-cinq/ai-agent-subsystem#245", "re-cinq/ai-agent-subsystem#246", "re-cinq/lore#2133", "adrs/ADR-031-agent-station-crds.md"]}
```

